# The five OECD principles and the curation of the data (generated by `cypmode/challenge/oecd_principles.py`)

Each cell is read from a file of the project or computed by the module; the sources are named in the last column. The cross-validated numbers are estimates on the training data and not scores on the hidden labels, except where a row says that it reads the released labels.

Abbreviations: AUC, area under the receiver operating characteristic curve; AUPRC, area under the precision–recall curve; ECFP4, extended-connectivity fingerprints of diameter 4; MCC, Matthews correlation coefficient; TDI, time-dependent inhibition; z0, the cut on the confidence of the label (1.0 or 1.96).

| principle | isoform | evidence | source |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| 1. A defined endpoint | CYP3A4 | time-dependent inhibition of CYP3A4: positive when the pIC50 after pre-incubation exceeds the direct-inhibition pIC50 (floored at 4) by more than log10 2; the rule gives the given label for 2334 of 2334 compounds of the pool and for all 747 of the 750 released test labels for which both potencies are given (0 disagree, 3 cannot be computed). | audit section 4; tdi_targets.py; post_deadline tdi_question2a_agreement.csv |
| 2. An unambiguous algorithm | CYP3A4 | 28 members (default+all_survivors), a logistic blend of the inner out-of-fold scores with the penalty and its strength chosen on the inner folds, isotonic calibration, a call rate of 1.3 times the prevalence; every member, column set, hyperparameter, seed, and package version is in algorithm_manifest.json; the code is open, and each submitted file has a SHA-256 hash. | algorithm_manifest.json; manifest.json; nested_runners.py; final_tdi_build.py |
| 3. A defined domain of applicability | CYP3A4 | reliability by the nearest-training similarity of a compound (Tanimoto similarity of extended-connectivity fingerprints of diameter 4, ECFP4), bins supported when the lower end of a 95% interval over whole Butina clusters reaches AUC 0.60; 750 supported, 0 weak, 0 unsupported of 750 blinded compounds; < 0.3: n 165, AUC 0.783, supported; 0.3 to 0.4: n 670, AUC 0.813, supported; 0.4 to 0.5: n 968, AUC 0.810, supported; 0.5 to 0.6: n 410, AUC 0.851, supported; 0.6 to 0.7: n 219, AUC 0.838, supported; >= 0.7: n 116, AUC 0.887, supported. | applicability_domain.md; applicability_domain.py |
| 4. Goodness of fit, robustness, and predictivity | CYP3A4 | goodness of fit: the 23 candidates refitted on the pool score a mean AUC of 0.978 on the pool against 0.758 on held-out folds (z0 1.0), an optimism of 0.219 that the nested design removes; robustness: nested outer AUC 0.8338 (z0 1.0) and 0.8622 (z0 1.96), MCC at the transferred rate 0.476 and 0.539; permuted labels: AUC 0.5096 (range 0.4802 to 0.5351), MCC +0.0020 (range -0.0376 to +0.0287) / AUC 0.5096 (range 0.4942 to 0.5201), MCC -0.0043 (range -0.0374 to +0.0404); ratio of columns to compounds: the widest candidate reads 5863 columns for 1493 to 2334 compounds; the extra-column, effective-dimension and fewer-column analyses are in descriptor_ratio.log; predictivity: on the labels released after the deadline, scored by the organisers' own code: MCC 0.467 (standard deviation 0.033) for CYP3A4; macro MCC 0.3723; on the second data set (TDC CYP3A4_Veith, official protocol) the test AUPRC is 0.891 against a published median of 0.862 (19 entries): ABOVE THE MEDIAN. | goodness_of_fit.csv; nested results of the final build; permutation_control logs; post_deadline outputs; external_dataset.log; descriptor_ratio.log |
| 5. A mechanistic interpretation, if possible | CYP3A4 | 4 of 26 alerts and motifs are enriched among the positives and 0 are depleted (Fisher, Holm p < 0.05); the largest odds ratios: terminal_alkene (6.23), methylenedioxyphenyl (5.17), cyclopropylamine (2.76), methoxy_aryl (1.87); depleted: none; share of the gain of one LightGBM model by block: rdkit_desc 46%, avalon 18%, erg 13%, morgan_c2 10%. | alert_enrichment.csv; block_gain.csv; feature_store.py (the alerts) |
| 1. A defined endpoint | CYP2D6 | time-dependent inhibition of CYP2D6: positive when the pIC50 after pre-incubation exceeds the direct-inhibition pIC50 (floored at 4) by more than log10 2; the rule gives the given label for 1493 of 1493 compounds of the pool and for all 741 of the 748 released test labels for which both potencies are given (0 disagree, 7 cannot be computed). | audit section 4; tdi_targets.py; post_deadline tdi_question2a_agreement.csv |
| 2. An unambiguous algorithm | CYP2D6 | 23 members (default), a logistic blend of the inner out-of-fold scores with the penalty and its strength chosen on the inner folds, isotonic calibration, a call rate of 1.0 times the prevalence; every member, column set, hyperparameter, seed, and package version is in algorithm_manifest.json; the code is open, and each submitted file has a SHA-256 hash. | algorithm_manifest.json; manifest.json; nested_runners.py; final_tdi_build.py |
| 3. A defined domain of applicability | CYP2D6 | reliability by the nearest-training similarity of a compound (Tanimoto similarity of extended-connectivity fingerprints of diameter 4, ECFP4), bins supported when the lower end of a 95% interval over whole Butina clusters reaches AUC 0.60; 0 supported, 599 weak, 151 unsupported of 750 blinded compounds; < 0.3: n 395, AUC 0.527, weak; 0.3 to 0.4: n 585, AUC 0.608, weak; 0.4 to 0.5: n 226, AUC 0.667, weak; 0.5 to 0.6: n 113, AUC 0.714, weak; 0.6 to 0.7: n 13, AUC not estimated, unsupported; >= 0.7: n 15, AUC not estimated, unsupported. | applicability_domain.md; applicability_domain.py |
| 4. Goodness of fit, robustness, and predictivity | CYP2D6 | goodness of fit: the 23 candidates refitted on the pool score a mean AUC of 0.992 on the pool against 0.684 on held-out folds (z0 1.0), an optimism of 0.308 that the nested design removes; robustness: nested outer AUC 0.7312 (z0 1.0) and 0.7536 (z0 1.96), MCC at the transferred rate 0.167 and 0.204; permuted labels: AUC 0.5012 (range 0.4770 to 0.5265), MCC +0.0196 (range -0.0069 to +0.0509) / AUC 0.4987 (range 0.4434 to 0.5392), MCC -0.0045 (range -0.0380 to +0.0602); ratio of columns to compounds: the widest candidate reads 5863 columns for 1493 to 2334 compounds; the extra-column, effective-dimension and fewer-column analyses are in descriptor_ratio.log; predictivity: on the labels released after the deadline, scored by the organisers' own code: MCC 0.277 (standard deviation 0.068) for CYP2D6; macro MCC 0.3723; on the second data set (TDC CYP2D6_Veith, official protocol) the test AUPRC is 0.727 against a published median of 0.649 (19 entries): ABOVE THE MEDIAN. | goodness_of_fit.csv; nested results of the final build; permutation_control logs; post_deadline outputs; external_dataset.log; descriptor_ratio.log |
| 5. A mechanistic interpretation, if possible | CYP2D6 | 1 of 24 alerts and motifs is enriched among the positives and 1 is depleted (Fisher, Holm p < 0.05); the largest odds ratios: methylenedioxyphenyl (4.89); depleted: imidazole_Nsub (0.54); share of the gain of one LightGBM model by block: rdkit_desc 39%, avalon 20%, erg 16%, morgan_c2 9%. | alert_enrichment.csv; block_gain.csv; feature_store.py (the alerts) |

